Subject: AOT generator skeleton: digest binding, entry/exit and the runtime ABI

What this does
  Entry/exit and the runtime ABI.

Why we need it
  And this turns that into a linkable unit the real call path can enter and leave.

What it adds
  `quickjs-aot-rt.h` (the generated-code ABI: `JSAotEntry`/`JSAotFn`/`QJS_AOT_ABI`, the `QJS_AOT_COLD_RET`/`QJS_AOT_SUSPEND` sentinels, `qjs_aot_step`/`qjs_aot_code`/`qjs_aot_ret`/`qjs_aot_unwind`), `quickjs-aot-gen.h` (the host generator interface used by the unshipped `tools/aot/qjsaot.c`), `JSFunctionBytecode.aot_fn`/`aot_state`, the AOT entry in `js_regvm_execute`, the runtime block (weak unit table, `aot_unit_present`, `js_aot_bind`, `QJS_AOT_STATS` counters), the generator collection block, and the `QJS_AOT`/`QJS_AOT_GEN`/`QJS_AOT_VERIFY` knobs.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
